ermination of water/octan-1-ol partition coefficient (log P). Briefly, about 3 μmol of complexes 1–6 was ultrasonicated for 30 min in 20 ml of 0.2 m NaCl solution in octanol-saturated water (NaCl was added to suppress hydrolysis). A 5-ml portion of supernatant (obtained by 5 min centrifugation) represented the solution for determination of [M]OSWb [i.e. metal (Ru, Os or Ir) concentration before partition]. Another 5-ml portion of supernatant was added to 5 ml of water-saturated octanol, shaken intensively at laboratory temperature for 2 hr and separated carefully. The metal concentration was determined by ICP-MS. The equation log P = log([M]WSO/[M]OSWa) was used, where [M]OSWa stand for the M concentration after the partition and [M]WSO = [M]OSWb - [M]OSWa. The experiment was conducted in triplicate and the results are given as arithmetic mean ± SD."}]}